1337x_Scrapper
https://github.com/PyFolk-Devs/1337x_Scrapper

Marquo began as a derivative of this project, a single-file command-line torrent
search tool. Its own file is no longer here, but the function that reads 1337x's
results table is derived from it: the row and cell selectors, the order the cells
are read in, the names the values are held under, and the predicate that finds the
size cell are all substantially as that project wrote them.

That function lives in sources/x1337.py. The Android app's src/sources/x1337.ts is
a port of the same code and carries the same history.

Everything else here - the API, the frontend, the other indexers, the analysis of a
torrent's details, the smart-TV rating, the filters and the tests - was written for
this project.

